# Pinned from the real red run of 2026-08-02 with the injection applied.
#
# The injection is two hunks, one per blind channel:
#
#   drivers/tmux.rs — `pane_activity_watch` returns before it opens anything,
#   so the tmux transport publishes no continuous pane event of any kind. The
#   FIFO, the throttle and the `pipe-pane` plumbing stay exactly where the fix
#   put them, unreachable.
#
#   daemon/supervisor.rs — the open-turn consult and the pane-pid resolution
#   are rmux-only again, as JQ8AV shipped them. `PaneMux`, `pane_content` and
#   `pane_pid` keep working for rmux and a tmux run reaches none of it.
#
# Together that is the state the task names: on the shipped default driver a
# provider-bound turn at ~0% cpu with no tool calls has NO evidence channel
# able to see it, and the clock releases it at the deadline.

exit: 101

# The daemon half: the very first compressed window kills the network-waiting
# tmux stub, and the tombstone is the FZB6T/RB1ZN/SZJ2B shape.
contains: quiet window 0: a provider-bound network-waiting tmux turn was stall-released
contains: stall_timeout_exceeded

# The driver half: the watcher publishes nothing at all for a real, writing
# pane, so its event channel closes before any activity arrives.
contains: tmux_pane_activity_publishes_raw_byte_counts_from_a_real_pane
contains: the pane event channel closed before any activity

# Exactly one test per binary, and both binaries. A suite that collapses
# wholesale is a different failure and has not reproduced this defect; a run
# that reddens only one target has reproduced only half of it. The filtered-out
# counts are deliberately not pinned — they move with every unrelated test.
contains: test result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed
contains: error: 2 targets failed:
contains: `-p orgasmic-daemon --lib`
contains: `-p orgasmic-drivers --lib`
